  "id": "u09-l05",
  "unit": "u09-past",
  "title": "I didn't",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "To say 'didn't' or 'haven't', Bengali takes the **present** form and adds **-নি** (*-ni*), written joined to the verb:\n\n- করি → **করিনি** 'I didn't do / haven't done'\n- খাই → **খাইনি** 'I didn't eat / haven't eaten'\n- খাও → **খাওনি** 'you didn't eat'\n- আসে → **আসেনি** 'he hasn't come'\n\nDon't say ~~করলাম না~~ for a simple 'I didn't do it' — it sounds like 'I chose not to'.\n\n**এখনো** 'yet / still' pairs naturally with -নি: **আমি এখনো খাইনি** 'I haven't eaten yet'. Short answer: **এখনো না** 'not yet'. **ইতিমধ্যে** 'already' is a bit formal.",
